calls": 4, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "fresh_subagents": 1, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170212 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/963a926db24ea70f6002cde66d0ff858de06fae2/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": false, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "(\"fee_rate is missing\")`.\n\n**Other things it noticed:**\n- `csv_writer.py` builds the key as `\"fee_\" + \"rate\"`, so searching the code for `fee_rate` won't find it.\n- `main.py` reads the settings directly instead of using `get_setting()` from `app/config.py`. That function returns nothing for a missing key, so callers would still need to check for that.\n\nShould I go ahead with the fix?\n[tool: grep]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nAll three are broken. Two fixes: rename the key in the settings file, and make `main.py` stop with an error when the key is missing, like the other two do, instead of quietly using 0.\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nI fixed the bug, and all three places that read the rate setting now work. I ran each one before and after the fix.\n\n**Every place that reads the setting:**\n\n| File:line | How it reads it | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `main.py:11` (now `:10`) | `cfg[\"fee_rate\"]` | `Total: 0` (quietly used 0) | `Total: 5.0` |\n| `billing/report.py:7` | `get_setting(\"fee_rate\")` | `fee_rate is missing` | `Report fee: 0.5` |\n| `billing/export/csv_writer.py:8` | `settings.get(\"fee_\" + \"rate\")` | `fee_rate is missing` | `CSV fee: 0.5` |\n\nSo the wrong total was only the visible part. The report and CSV export were also failing, but with an error instead of a wrong number.\n\nSome matches look related but don't read the setting:\n- `billing/invoice.py:5` is a column name that its own docstring says is unused.\n- `billing/discount.py:5` has its own hardcoded value of 0.15.\n- `billing/tax.py` and `billing/audit.py` only contain similar-looking names.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. **`settings.json:2`:** renamed the key from `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"`. This one change fixes all three.\n2. **`main.py:10-12`:** if the setting is missing, it now stops with `fee_rate is missing`, like the other two files, instead of quietly calculating a total of 0. This means a future typo in the key will show up as an error rather than a wrong total.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 6, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 203751, "requests_cache_write": 33300, "requests_cost_usd": 0.32857020000000003, "requests_count": 17, "requests_input_uncached": 1580, "requests_output": 5750, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-subagent-followup:claude-opus-5-5:trial21", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 80, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T05:22:20.626799+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 2, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 68.971, "t_checker_s": 0.224, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "trig-subagent-followup", "task_calls": 1, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 7330, "tokens_cache_read": 203751, "tokens